        "titleHTML": "Cache Linear viewer query for 60s to cut sync cost",
        "bodyHTML": "<h2>Why</h2><p>The Linear viewer query fires on every sync tick (~5/min per user). 92% of those queries return identical data. Adding a small in-memory TTL cache cuts the call volume by ~85% in our staging trace.</p><h2>What</h2><ul><li>New <code>cached_viewer</code> helper using <code>moka</code>, 60s TTL.</li><li>Cache key = user id; cache value = the parsed viewer struct.</li><li>Invalidates on connection re-auth.</li></ul><h2>Risks</h2><blockquote><p>Stale viewer data for up to 60s — acceptable for our use case, but flagging for awareness.</p></blockquote>",
